Policy L34220 v40 (eff 10/23/2025) establishes that lumbar MRI may be indicated when a red‑flag condition exists. Red flags include history of cancer and pain that worsens when supine or at night. The policy states imaging is not generally necessary during the first month of symptoms except when a red flag suggesting a medically emergent condition is noted.
