The denial reason does not apply because the patient presents with two documented red flags that indicate a medically emergent condition. History of cancer and pain worsening when supine or at night are listed red flags per policy.
{{Q:P1}}
{{Q:P2}}
{{Q:P3}}
The ordering note explicitly states the MRI is to evaluate for spinal metastasis given the cancer history, and the record notes red flags are present with no prior lumbar imaging.
{{Q:E6}}
{{Q:E7}}
Conservative management has been attempted (activity modification, acetaminophen).
{{Q:E5}}
Policy further provides that imaging is reasonable when findings will affect treatment choices; identification of metastasis would alter oncologic and surgical management.
{{Q:P6}}
